course: dictionary
lesson: 1544
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Chalk is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which is its context. «Chalk drawings belong on your own driveway or a quiet path, never on the road where cars come.» Drawings and driveways tell you that chalk here is a stick you draw with.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. Could you put a stick you draw with into the sentence and have it still make sense? Yes, so you have the right meaning. A rock would not fit at all.
explain: Chalk can also be a soft white rock, like the White Cliffs of Dover. Chalk is a verb too: to chalk something is to write or draw it with chalk. «Ya-las, water is ending, is chalked on the big stone water-tank.»
fact: Chalk is a soft white rock made from tiny shells of sea creatures.
fact: A stick of chalk is made from this rock or similar stuff, and teachers use it on blackboards.
fact: To chalk something means to write or draw it with chalk, as in «chalk drawings» on the pavement.
fact: Chalk and cheese means two things that are very different.
fact: Eggshell and chalk are both calcium carbonate, so they fizz in vinegar.
exercise: «Chalk drawings belong on your own driveway or a quiet path.» In this sentence, what is chalk? | A soft white rock from the sea | A kind of wet paint | A type of cliff | *A stick you draw with
exercise: «Mia chalked her name on the board.» What does chalked mean? | Washed away with water | Rubbed out | *Wrote or drew with chalk | Painted with a big brush
exercise: «The White Cliffs of Dover are made of chalk.» What is chalk here? | A stick for the blackboard | A kind of paint | *A soft white rock | A type of tree
test: «Sam and Jo are like chalk and cheese: he loves maths, she loves painting.» What does chalk and cheese mean? | Lots of chalk | Good to eat together | *Very different | Very similar
test: «Eggshell and chalk fizz in vinegar.» Why do they both fizz? | They are both made of metal | *They are both calcium carbonate | They are both wet | They are both made of wood
exam: In «"Ya-las", water is ending, is chalked on the big stone water-tank», what does chalked mean? | Painted red | Scrubbed off with soap | *Written with chalk | Carved deep into the stone
